codex
**Findings**

- Line 423: input `"'NCT12345678': { name: 'ALPHA', snippet: 'NCT12345678: BETA' }"`; consequence: `check_26` can only `pass` and return `[]`, so the acronym-drift check cannot fail.

- Line 557: input `"<script>const x = `${foo`;</script>"`; consequence: `check_38` never appends a finding, so the claimed P0 template-literal check cannot fail.

- Line 32: input `"pmid: 'NaN'"`; consequence: `PMID_RE` captures only digits, so `check_14` cannot report the documented non-numeric PMID strings.

- Line 35: input `'<a href="missing.html#top">x</a>'`; consequence: `check_05` ignores broken local links with fragments or queries because the regex requires the extension immediately before the quote.

- Line 141: input `"{{token}}"`; consequence: `check_06` misses the lowercase placeholder form named in its own docstring.

- Line 216: input `"AUTO_INCLUDE_TRIAL_IDS = new Set(['NCT00000001','NCT00000002']); realData: { 'NCT00000002': { snippet: 'see NCT00000001' } }, async init"`; consequence: `check_10` accepts an AUTO_INCLUDE id merely mentioned inside a value, not present as a `realData` key.

- Line 291: input `'<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src \\'self\\'; img-src https://cdn.bad.test"><script src="https://cdn.bad.test/app.js"></script>'`; consequence: `check_16` treats a host allowed only for images as allowed for scripts.

- Line 463: input `"<script>const RapidMetadata = {}; RapidMeta.init();</script>"`; consequence: `check_31` mistakes a prefix name for the actual `RapidMeta` binding and misses an undefined global.

- Line 563: input `"<button><svg></svg></button>"`; consequence: `check_39` misses icon-only buttons with no text and no `aria-label`.

No proven defect found here for: string-a-fix-removes probe, self-satisfied idempotency guard, CRLF/LF text comparison, merged-cell/off-by-one tabulation, zero conflated with absent, negation dropped, or wrapper-status reporting.
